{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2123","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Blackboard Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initially, the integers from $$$0$$$ to $$$n-1$$$ are written on a blackboard."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one round, "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Alice chooses an integer $$$a$$$ on the blackboard and erases it; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" then Bob chooses an integer $$$b$$$ on the blackboard such that $$$a+b \\equiv 3 \\pmod 4$$$$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ and erases it. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Rounds take place in succession until a player is unable to make a move — the first player who is unable to make a move loses. Determine who wins with optimal play. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$We define that $$$x\\equiv y\\pmod m$$$ whenever $$$x-y$$$ is an integer multiple of $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 100$$$)  — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\leq n \\leq 100$$$) — the number of integers written on the blackboard."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output on a single line \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if Alice wins with optimal play, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bob"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if Bob wins with optimal play."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case (upper or lower). For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aLiCe"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"alice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ALICE"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"alICE"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2\n4\n5\n7\n100\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nAlice\nBob\nAlice\nAlice\nBob\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, suppose Alice chooses $$$0$$$, then Bob cannot choose any number so Alice wins immediately."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, suppose Alice chooses $$$0$$$, then Bob can choose $$$3$$$. Then suppose Alice chooses $$$2$$$, then Bob can choose $$$1$$$. Then Alice has no numbers remaining, so Bob wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2123A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2123/problem/A"}